BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23234Z
UID:J31BphdXVn-8225536925@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260427
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501
SUMMARY:SPJ Ethics Week
URL:http://www.spj.org/spj-ethics-week/
DESCRIPTION:This year’s Ethics Week focuses on potentially improving the SPJ Code of Ethics\, America’s most influential media ethics code. SPJ wants feedback from the public\, journalists and those close to journalism to revise the Code for just the sixth time in its 100-year history.

The SPJ Ethics Committee\, a group of current and former journalists\, journalism researchers\, educators and advocates\, is reviewing the Code. By the end of 2026\, the committee aims to present its recommendations for consideration by SPJ’s board and members.
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23235Z
UID:0Bmznnyn2c-8224921144@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T213000
SUMMARY:Stillwater Awards Ceremony
URL:http://www.eventbrite.com/e/stillwater-awards-ceremony-tickets-1985385526555?aff=oddtdtcreator
DESCRIPTION:Join us to honor the best stories and courageous journalists behind prison walls from 2025 at the Stillwater Awards!

Celebrate incarcerated journalists and their work.

The Stillwater Awards honor excellence in one of the most challenging fields of journalism: reporting and telling true stories from behind prison walls. We’ll be recognizing the important work of incarcerated writers whose stories shed light on life inside and challenge the public’s understanding of the prison legal system.

Join us for an inspiring virtual ceremony where we’ll announce the winners\, share their messages\, and celebrate alongside many of their family members and friends.

The event will be hosted by Michael Anguille (Stillwater Awards Director) and Kashawn Taylor (Prison Journalism Project Audience Engagement Fellow).

The Stillwater Awards are presented by the Society of Professional Journalists and Prison Journalism Project.
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23236Z
UID:soB99C81mb-8225609445@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T200000
SUMMARY:Ethics Week webinar: Blurred Lines: Should journalists be defined and regulated?
URL:http://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_lBQNRKTTScuTAF_HaRa0Zw
DESCRIPTION:The SPJ Ethics Committee will host a virtual panel discussion\, “Blurred Lines: Should journalists be defined and regulated?” The panel will examine how to identify reporters and ethical journalism in a sea of digital content creators\, activists masquerading as reporters and misinformation. Panelists include Olivia Hicks\, The Minnesota Star Tribune sports reporter and Gen Z journalist who writes about young people and their understanding of journalism; Liz Kelly Nelson\, founder of Project C\, which trains independent news creators\, and former executive at Gannett and Vox; Aaron Parnas\, digital news creator and “Newsfluencer” with 8 million-plus social media followers;  and Erik Ugland\, Marquette University associate professor who studies how journalists are defined. SPJ Ethics Committee Chair Dan Axelrod will moderate.
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23237Z
UID:nQQQFuUSOo-8225609224@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T200000
SUMMARY:Ethics Week webinar: Why Revise the SPJ Ethics Code Now, and What Should Be Improved?
URL:http://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_YFYanNzHQciYp9axzWCzIw
DESCRIPTION:The Ethics Committee will host “Why Revise the SPJ Ethics Code Now\, and What Should Be Improved?” Committee members will discuss Code revision-related comments and suggestions emailed to ethics@spj.org and submitted via surveys for the public\, journalists and those close to journalism.
LOCATION:
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23238Z
UID:Rsd4Z2Vzot-8223722574@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T183000
SUMMARY:World Press Freedom Day Reception at the National Press Club
URL:http://www.eventbrite.com/e/world-press-freedom-day-reception-tickets-1987397248670?aff=oddtdtcreator
DESCRIPTION:Join us in recognition of World Press Freedom Day: A moment to celebrate the essential role of a free press and to stand in clear-eyed solidarity with journalists around the world.

This year\, we come together with both pride and urgency.

Across the globe and here at home\, journalists are doing extraordinary work under increasing pressure -- facing threats\, arrests\, restrictions\, and a rapidly shifting information landscape. Yet\, every day\, they continue to report\, investigate\, and inform their communities with courage and integrity.

This reception is an opportunity to pause and recognize that work -- to connect with colleagues\, partners\, and advocates committed to press freedom -- and to reaffirm our shared responsibility to support and protect it. 

The evening will feature brief remarks\, community\, and conversation\, highlighting both the challenges ahead and the enduring strength of a free and independent press. We’ll also introduce our 2026 Press Freedom Fellow Cohort\, journalists who have experienced obstacles but who persist in their pursuit of journalism. 


LOCATION:National Press Building\, Washington\, DC\, USA
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T23239Z
UID:1oCZ107DJK-8224845011@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T113000
SUMMARY:Staying Safe in the Field 
URL:http://calendar.spjnetwork.org/displayevent.php?e=1oCZ107DJK-8224845011
DESCRIPTION:Join the SPJ Georgia Pro Chapter for part 2 of their “Safety & Security for Journalists” workshop series -- Staying Safe in the Field.

This in-person\, hands-on\, interactive training will give you practical tips on physical safety -- whether you’re reporting on conflicts and civil unrest\, working the general assignment beat or editing in the newsroom.

Our instructor brings 20+ years of combined experience in public safety and corporate security and will cover situational awareness\, active attacker response\, first aid basics and protest & field safety.

Pastries and coffee will be served. Parking is free. 

This event is for SPJ members only. RSVP is required at spjgeorgia@gmail.com

LOCATION:Georgia Public Broadcasting\, Atlanta\, GA
END:VEVENT





BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20170606T232310Z
UID:naJjuQ4vP2-8224251358@spjnetwork.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T150000
SUMMARY:News Reimagined: The Creator Journalism Summit
URL:http://www.eventbrite.com/e/news-reimagined-the-creator-journalism-summit-tickets-1986838877567?aff=oddtdtcreator&#38;keep_tld=true
DESCRIPTION:Journalism isn’t just evolving. It’s being rebuilt in real time. News Reimagined is where that transformation comes to life. This one-day experience brings together journalists\, creators\, and newsroom leaders who are figuring out how to grow audiences\, build trust\, and make this work sustainable.

We kick things off with mainstage speakers Bianca Graulau and Nick Valencia\, whose independent reporting has reached millions and redefined what it means to connect with an audience. They’ll set the tone for a day focused on bold ideas\, real talk\, and practical takeaways.

Whether you’re a newsroom leader hoping to work with creators or a creator-journalist who wants to scale up your business\, we have you covered.

For newsrooms & publishers:

You know creators matter. Now what?

This track gets into the how. What does smart partnership actually look like? How do you budget for it? What are you paying for\, and how do you measure success? We’ll dig into real examples\, unpack agreements and contracts\, and tackle the big questions around ethics\, standards\, and trust when working with creators who may not come from traditional newsrooms.

For journalists & creators:

You’ve got the skills. It’s time to build something of your own.

This track is all about turning your journalism into a sustainable business. Learn how to grow an audience\, choose the right platforms\, price your work\, negotiate with confidence\, and create multiple revenue streams. Whether you’re just starting out or scaling up\, you’ll leave with tools you can use immediately.

At its core\, this summit is about one thing: relationships. The future of journalism will be built through collaboration: between creators and newsrooms\, journalists and audiences\, ideas and opportunity. This is where those connections start.

Confirmed speakers include:

Bianca Graulau\, independent journalist from Puerto Rico
Michael Jones\, independent national political reporter\, Once Upon a Hill
S. Mitra Kalita\, co-founder/ CEO\, URL Media
Ryan Y. Kellett\, co-founder\, The Independent Journalism Atlas
Adrienne Johnson Martin\, co-executive director\, MLK50
Nick Valencia\, founder\, Nick Valencia News
Krysta Villeda\, chief operating officer\, Pulso
LOCATION:National Press Club\, Washington\, D.C.
END:VEVENT





